<!-- page: 1 -->

This is the main content\.

The “Header” style has a thick double red line top border\, but this should not be shown on this page as there is no header enabled in this section\.

There is a “first page header” which is not shown because the “different first page header” option was switched off\. The presence of this disabled header is what triggers fdo\#77844 resulting in the double red line being shown above this page\.

<!-- page: 2 -->

This page is in section 2\, which has the “different first page header” option enabled\, so it actually shows the first page header \(which was inherited from section 1\)\. The double red line should be shown above this page\.

<!-- page: 3 -->

This is the second page of section 2\. The double red line should be on this page too\, though its header is blank\, because of headers being enabled in this section by the presence of the first\-page header\.

<!-- page: 4 -->

This is section 3\. It has no headers and the page should have no lines at the top\.